OL,3,AGerman town bans 'stumbling stone'
OL,4,Amemorials to Nazi victims
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere has been a wave of criticism in
OL,7,FGermany after the town of Heidenau,
OL,8,Fnear Dresden in Saxony, decided to ban
OL,9,F"stumbling stone" memorials to victims
OL,10,Fof the Nazis.
OL,12,FGermany's Education Minister Karin
OL,13,FPrien told newspaper Bild that the ban
OL,14,Fwas a "scandal".
OL,16,FSince the 1990s, many towns in
OL,17,Fcountries across Europe, including in
OL,18,FGermany and Austria, have embedded
OL,19,Fsmall brass plaques in the streets in
OL,20,Fmemory of Jews and other victims of
OL,21,FNazi atrocities.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG11/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,0,100
